\": \"mol_013\",\n      \"incoming_reactions\": [\"rxn_009\", \"rxn_010\"],\n      \"outgoing_reactions\": [\"rxn_011\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}", "parsed_response": {"target_molecule": "L-Proline", "overall_strategy": "The network is centered on the only experimentally resolved prebiotic route to the proline skeleton: the Patel-type cyanosulfidic surface sequence from HCN, acetylene, NH3, and sulfide. To correct the balance problems of earlier coarse renderings, the route is expanded into explicit aldehyde, cyanohydrin, cyclic alpha-hydroxythioamide, thiolactam, imine, and aminonitrile nodes. Three chemically motivated choice points are encoded as parallel reactions: Cu-free vs Cu-accelerated aldehyde generation, Cu-free vs Cu-accelerated photodeoxygenation to the thiolactam, and late surface-photochemical vs hydrothermal H2/FeS/NiS desulfurization to the imine. No known prebiotic chemistry makes L-proline directly; therefore the target node is reached only after hydrolysis of proline aminonitrile and seed-dependent physical enantioenrichment, with the D-proline node used as the explicit non-target companion phase. Cyanamide diversion to arginine is acknowledged in reaction reasoning but omitted as a non-target sink.", "molecules": [{"id": "mol_001", "formula": "HCN", "iupac_name": "hydrogen cyanide", "common_name": "hydrogen cyanide", "inchi": null, "role": "starting", "environment_formed": null}, {"id": "mol_002", "formula": "C2H2", "iupac_name": "ethyne", "common_name": "acetylene", "inchi": null, "role": "starting", "environment_formed": null}, {"id": "mol_003", "formula": "NH3", "iupac_name": "azane", "common_name": "ammonia", "inchi": null, "role": "starting", "environment_formed": null}, {"id": "mol_004", "formula": "H2S", "iupac_name": "sulfane", "common_name": "hydrogen sulfide", "inchi": null, "role": "starting", "environment_formed": null}, {"id": "mol_005", "formula": "H2O", "iupac_name": "oxidane", "common_name": "water", "inchi": null, "role": "starting", "env